      "headline": "Direction is near-universal: 11/12 cells show positive forward excess return after a VIX spike. Raw 5% significance at 4 cells (thr30_H5, thr30_H60, thr35_H60, thr40_H60). Under strict FDR-5% multiple-testing correction NONE survive individually; under FDR-10% 3 survive (thr30_H5, thr35_H60, thr40_H60). The panic-entry edge is real in direction but small: it mostly rides SPY's baseline upward drift, and the durable component is a slow 3-month (H60) reversion premium that scales with panic depth, not an instant bounce. Statistically fragile at thresholds 35/40 where N is small (25 / 17 events).",
